        "raw_output": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"music_history\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_eea96da5ed6aec3e471036e5\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user has explored various genres and attended festivals, including an electronic music festival in 2017. They tried learning music theory in 2018 but found it unfulfilling, preferring emotional connection over technical analysis. They attempted researching historical music trends in 2020, which felt tedious. They also explored audio production techniques but found it a chore. They have created their own tracks, which brings joy and satisfaction. They watched a music documentary that felt unsatisfying. They have not played an instrument or composed in a formal sense, but they have engaged in creative activities like making playlists and creating original music. They have also blended nature sounds into their music, shared knowledge with young musicians, integrated their cultural heritage into compositions, developed an app to help others blend traditional and modern music, found a book on Pacific music that reignited their interest, participated in collaborative music sessions, and faced criticism when writing music reviews, which led them to focus on more personal expression.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s22\",\"s23\",\"s111\",\"s92\",\"s11\",\"s81\",\"s93\",\"s63\",\"s100\",\"s80\",\"s31\",\"s46\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s82\",\"s3\",\"s33\",\"s55\",\"s73\",\"s101\",\"s102\",\"s65\",\"s47\",\"s112\",\"s32\",\"s14\",\"s64\",\"s10\",\"s43\",\"s74\",\"s56\",\"s34\",\"s45\",\"s44\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"past\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user's statements across multiple conversations describe past experiences with music: attending an electronic music festival in 2017 (s31, s32), trying music theory in 2018 (s33, s34