inding historical research tedious (s10, s11, s12), and audio production feeling like a chore (s43, s44). They report enjoying live performances, exploring genres and cultural significance, album artwork and lyrics, and making playlists (s13, s14). They find fulfillment in creating their own tracks (s45, s46, s47) and connecting with their heritage through music (s55, s56). They also express disappointment with passive consumption like documentaries (s22, s23). No time, resource, or social constraints are mentioned.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"goals\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_93cb598879324dad103d61ea\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user's stated and implied goals for deepening their musical expression include: creating original music as a personal emotional outlet and form of self-expression; connecting with their cultural heritage and personal identity through music; exploring different genres and the cultural significance behind musical styles; attending live performances to feel the energy and connection; discovering album artwork, lyrics, and stories behind songs; making mood-based playlists; and sharing their work publicly to engage with listeners and collaborate. They explicitly reject technical dissection (music theory, audio production, historical research) as unfulfilling, preferring emotional and experiential engagement.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s22\",\"s23\",\"s11\",\"s12\",\"s46\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s55\",\"s47\",\"s59\",\"s14\",\"s10\",\"s43\",\"s56\",\"s45\",\"s44\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user consistently expresses a desire for emotional, creative, and culturally connected musical expression across multiple conversations. They describe finding joy in creating their own tracks (s45, s46), connecting with heritage (s55, s56), exploring genres and cultural significance (s13), attending live performances (s13), and discovering stories behind songs (s14). They also consider sharing work publicly (s59). They explicitly reject technical approaches like music theory (s3, s4), audio production (s43, s44), and historical research (s10, s11, s12) as stressful or unfulfilling. The summary captures these positive goals and negative experiences as a coherent whole.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"response\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_5943dc85f20743e5562cad6c\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"Collaborating with others who share your musical interests can also be a rewarding path. A user found fulfillment through working with musicians from diverse backgrounds, mixing traditional and electronic elements to expand their creative horizons. Such group efforts can enhance not only your musical explorations but also build lasting relationships, as you contribute unique perspectives to a collective musical vision.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s81\",\"s100\",\"s80\",\"s46\",\"s13\",\"s82\",\"s55\",\"s73\",\"s101\",\"s14\",\"s74\",\"s56\",\"s45\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {\"music_history\":2,\"current_constraints\":1,\"goals\":1},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user's history and goals strongly align with option (c). They have found fulfillment in collaborative music sessions (s100, s101), integrating cultural heritage (s55, s56), developing an app to blend traditional and modern music (s80, s81, s82), and teaching young musicians (s73, s74). They enjoy creating original tracks (s45, s46) and exploring genres and cultural significance (s13, s14). They explicitly reject technical/analytical approaches (music theory, audio production, historical research) as unfulfilling, which eliminates options (b) and (d). Option (a) is generic and does not leverage the user's demonstrated passion for collaboration and cultural fusion. Option (c) directly matches the user's positive experiences and stated goals of collaborative, culturally-connected, creative expression.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"audit_verdict\": \"supported\"\n}",
